{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,17]],"date-time":"2026-09-17T02:43:34Z","timestamp":1789613014089,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":70,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,10]],"date-time":"2024-01-10T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1704844800000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":9,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Global Change Biology"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Droughts have been implicated as the main driver behind recent vegetation die\u2010off and are projected to drive greater mortality under future climate change. Understanding the coupling relationship between vegetation and drought has been of great global interest. Currently, the coupling relationship between vegetation and drought is mainly evaluated by correlation coefficients or regression slopes. However, the optimal drought timescale of vegetation response to drought, as a key indicator reflecting vegetation sensitivity to drought, has largely been ignored. Here, we apply the optimal drought timescale identification method to examine the change in coupling between vegetation and drought over the past three decades (1982\u20132015) with long\u2010term satellite\u2010derived Normalized Difference Vegetation Index and Standardized Precipitation\u2010Evapotranspiration Index data. We find substantial increasing response of vegetation to drought timescales globally, and the correlation coefficient between vegetation and drought under optimal drought timescale overall declines between 1982 and 2015. This decrease in vegetation\u2013drought coupling is mainly observed in regions with water deficit, although its initial correlation is relatively high. However, vegetation in water\u2010surplus regions, with low coupling in earlier stages, is prone to show an increasing trend. The observed changes may be driven by the increasing trend of atmospheric CO\n                    <jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>\n                    . Our findings highlight more pressing drought risk in water\u2010surplus regions than in water\u2010deficit regions, which advances our understanding of the long\u2010term vegetation\u2013drought relationship and provides essential insights for mapping future vegetation sensitivity to drought under changing climate conditions.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1111\/gcb.17141","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,11]],"date-time":"2024-01-11T02:44:42Z","timestamp":1704941082000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":78,"title":["Declining coupling between vegetation and drought over the past three decades"],"prefix":"10.1111","volume":"30","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1050-9794","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Delong","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Geographical Sciences and Natural Resources Research, Chinese Academy of Sciences  Beijing China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7547-0221","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Li","family":"An","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Geographical Sciences and Natural Resources Research, Chinese Academy of Sciences  Beijing China"},{"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences  Beijing China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7529-454X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shuai","family":"Zhong","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Geographical Sciences and Natural Resources Research, Chinese Academy of Sciences  Beijing China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-4782-3779","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Lei","family":"Shen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Geographical Sciences and Natural Resources Research, Chinese Academy of Sciences  Beijing China"},{"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences  Beijing China"},{"name":"China\u2010Pakistan Joint Research Center on Earth Sciences, CAS\u2010HEC  Islamabad Pakistan"},{"name":"Key Laboratory of Carrying Capacity Assessment for Resource and Environment Ministry of Natural Resources of the People's Republic of China  Beijing China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0057-5483","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shuyao","family":"Wu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Center for Yellow River Ecosystem Products Shandong University  Qingdao Shandong China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,10]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_10_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/bioinformatics\/btq134"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41586\u2010018\u20100539\u20107"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111\/gcb.16867"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/joc.3887"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.aay5958"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s11749\u2010016\u20100481\u20107"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1023\/A:1010933404324"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.aat7631"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.1708984114"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41597\u2